Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: native backhaul state lines; an agent's uncertainty clears once observed again

The native backhaul module stopped measuring candidates in the geometry rooms: the
observations said candidate=unknown for every extender and backhaul-parent-handover's
extender_3 never moved, although the extenders' serving samples were fresh and weak
enough. Nothing said why. Every 30 s the module now says so in three lines: the counts
(nodes, backhaul APs, candidates, stations queried, uncertain agents with their
failures, BSSIDs dropped as ambiguous) and, per round, the reason each (candidate AP,
station) pair was skipped (no station, unknown parent, the AP's own station, another
channel or class, a stale or strong serving sample, no valid root path); the backhaul
AP table (BSSID, owner, operating class, channel); and each station's parent, serving
sample and whether it has a root path. They showed every station unrooted: the root
was an EMOSA agent in the gateway, whose 1905 interface carried its AL MAC in the
gateway's own namespace, so the controller had taken it for its co-located agent
(rdk-1004, 5 October 2026; fixed in EMOSA, emosa-lab spec 2.1 and finding 17).

An agent whose native move was not verified is marked uncertain: root_path() refuses
paths through it. The mark cleared only when the agent was later seen on that move's
exact target; when it ended anywhere else it stayed until em_ctrl restarted, and the
agent and everything under it were left out of every root path (seen for the pods EMOSA
serves, whose moves complete after the 15 s verification). It now also clears when the
agent is observed, fresh, on a known parent at least 30 s after the failed move: its
ancestry is known again, which is all the mark protects. The policy's own backoff is
unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/inc/em_ctrl.h	2026-10-04 23:55:22.914549263 -0700
+++ b/inc/em_ctrl.h	2026-10-04 23:55:44.119662140 -0700
@@ -95,6 +95,7 @@
     std::deque<backhaul_requested_t> m_backhaul_requested;
     int64_t m_backhaul_last_query = 0;
     uint64_t m_backhaul_round = 0;
+    int64_t m_backhaul_last_state = 0;   /* the periodic state line (every 30 s) */
     void handle_native_backhaul_tick();
     void collect_native_backhaul_refresh(const em_backhaul::snapshot &network, int64_t now,
         std::vector<std::vector<unsigned char>> &outgoing);
--- a/src/ctrl/em_backhaul_ctrl.cpp	2026-10-04 23:55:22.922549306 -0700
+++ b/src/ctrl/em_backhaul_ctrl.cpp	2026-10-05 07:58:39.092319868 -0700
@@ -147,6 +147,19 @@
                     static_cast<long long>(now - iterator->second.sent));
                 m_backhaul_policy.attempted(iterator->first, now, false);
                 iterator = m_backhaul_uncertain.erase(iterator);
+            } else if (current != network.nodes.end() && network.aps.count(current->second.parent_bssid) &&
+                current->second.serving.fresh(now) && now - iterator->second.sent >= 30000 &&
+                current->second.serving.observed >= iterator->second.sent + 30000) {
+                /* The agent never reached the target, but it is observed again, fresh, on a
+                 * known parent 30 s after the failed move: its ancestry is known, which is all
+                 * the mark protects. Kept, the mark excluded the agent and everything under it
+                 * from every root path until em_ctrl restarted (rdk-1004, 5 Oct 2026). The
+                 * policy's own backoff for the agent stays. */
+                em_printfout("Native backhaul uncertainty cleared agent=%s parent=%s target=%s elapsed_ms=%lld",
+                    backhaul_label(iterator->first).c_str(), backhaul_label(current->second.parent_bssid).c_str(),
+                    backhaul_label(iterator->second.request.target).c_str(),
+                    static_cast<long long>(now - iterator->second.sent));
+                iterator = m_backhaul_uncertain.erase(iterator);
             } else ++iterator;
         }
         for (const auto &uncertain : m_backhaul_uncertain)
@@ -245,6 +258,11 @@
             }
         }
         if (now - m_backhaul_last_query >= 4000) {
+            size_t queried_stations = 0;
+            /* why each (candidate AP, station) pair was not queried: no station, unknown parent,
+             * the AP's own station, another channel or class, a stale or strong serving sample,
+             * no valid root path; then the pairs queried */
+            unsigned int skipped[7] = {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
             m_backhaul_last_query = now;
             ++m_backhaul_round;
             for (const auto &entry : network.nodes) {
@@ -289,22 +307,61 @@
                 for (const auto &candidate : network.nodes) {
                     const auto &station = candidate.second;
                     const auto parent = network.aps.find(station.parent_bssid);
-                    if (station.al == network.root || station.al == ap.al || station.sta.empty() ||
-                        parent == network.aps.end() || parent->second.al == ap.al ||
-                        parent->second.channel != ap.channel || parent->second.op_class != ap.op_class ||
-                        !station.serving.fresh(now) || station.serving.rcpi >= 100) continue;
+                    if (station.al == network.root || station.al == ap.al || station.sta.empty()) {
+                        ++skipped[0];
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                    if (parent == network.aps.end()) { ++skipped[1]; continue; }
+                    if (parent->second.al == ap.al) { ++skipped[2]; continue; }
+                    if (parent->second.channel != ap.channel || parent->second.op_class != ap.op_class) {
+                        ++skipped[3];
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                    if (!station.serving.fresh(now) || station.serving.rcpi >= 100) { ++skipped[4]; continue; }
                     const auto route = em_backhaul::root_path(network, ap.al, station.al, now);
-                    if (!route.valid) continue;
+                    if (!route.valid) { ++skipped[5]; continue; }
+                    ++skipped[6];
                     query.stations[station.sta] = station.parent_bssid;
                     payload.insert(payload.end(), station.sta.begin(), station.sta.end());
                 }
                 if (query.stations.empty()) continue;
+                queried_stations += query.stations.size();
                 payload[3] = static_cast<unsigned char>(query.stations.size());
                 const unsigned short mid = get_next_msg_id();
                 m_backhaul_queries[mid] = query;
                 outgoing.push_back(em_backhaul::frame(ap.al, controller, em_msg_type_unassoc_sta_link_metrics_query,
                     mid, em_tlv_type_unassoc_sta_link_metric_query, payload));
             }
+            if (now - m_backhaul_last_state >= 30000) {
+                /* what decides whether candidates are measured at all: the model's nodes and
